    "authored-5": {
      "id": "authored-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision: one directory under catalog/ owns each manifest, canonical prompt, context, and state. The canonical PromptDocument is the only system-prompt source; prompt/system.md is derived. Why: keeping the bundle together makes agent behavior inspectable and avoids host-side prompt assembly. Applies to current and future catalog agents."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-6": {
      "id": "authored-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Knowledge and Live State"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-7": {
      "id": "authored-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision: context loads the shared native Docs guidance plus local tool/state references, while state renders session-specific target text, revisions, diffs, and the request queue. Why: reference knowledge changes with the docs and live state changes with each session. Applies to catalog context/state sidecars and tests."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-8": {
      "id": "authored-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Kernel Save Adapter"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "authored-9": {
      "id": "authored-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision: accepted proposals save through the Kernel catalog adapter into the shared authoring store. Kernel retains registry refresh, database provenance, and next-run prompt freezing. Why: direct external writes and staged internal review need the same file-level conflict and recovery behavior without sharing a model lifecycle."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
